WEBVTT

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.530
I am not a zookeeper.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:28.700
I am...

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.990
Why...

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:08.780
Does the Blue Impulse Custard
Castella Manju go well with coffee?

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.990
Or perhaps black tea?

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.780
Hasn't that man been coming here
every day?

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:18.040
He always buys local sweets.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.170
They have quite a decent selection.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.430
So the first is cancelled, ey?

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.560
I wonder if they're doing well...

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:42.400
Welp, there's nothing I can do
for them anyway.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:43.480
Here you go.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.900
Have a drink.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:46.900
Really?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.610
Ooh, the limited hand-picked kiwi flavor!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:50.780
Did you know

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.530
that it is said kiwifruit tastes better
with the skin left on?

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.490
Huh? Shouldn't you peel it off?

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.830
They say the skin tastes sweeter.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.760
The skin's sweeter, eh?

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.180
Wait a moment. Just wait a moment.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.980
Miss, would you so kindly give
that kiwi-flavored Joa to me?

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.230
-Huh?
-Not for free of course.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.730
Would you consider trading it for this
Blue Impulse Custard Castella Manju?

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:33.070
Sorry. I'm not a fan of custard.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:36.620
Nooooo!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.540
I got one!

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.000
That's amazing, Amakasu!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:49.460
Our first catch of protein,
only five days into our survival training.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:55.130
Just two more days
until we leave our lives here behind.

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:58.470
They've become fast friends.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.220
It doesn't seem like
they want to go home just yet.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.390
But,

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.020
F-2 won't play with them.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.230
Just like its pilot.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.860
Even though
the sun's not shining much today,

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.940
it must be hot wearing that armor
this whole time, right?

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:15.490
Surely it's burning up.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:20.200
Wearing that armor is the same
as being cooked on a teppan grill.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:23.410
Ah!

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.040
F-2!

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.250
I'm sorry, F-2!

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.920
For not realizing it sooner!

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.340
Huh?

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.090
It's not as hot as I thought.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.640
Wow, you're right.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.720
I wonder if it's some sort
of special metal.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:44.480
It endures the scorching heat
as if inside a Brazen Bull.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:48.150
This awkward manliness
is just like that of Ken.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:49.520
Who is Ken?

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.900
Ah, don't mind me.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:54.440
I'm not sure why,

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:59.410
but it feels like "Ken" would be
a much nicer name than F-2.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.370
Ken,

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:05.500
Hoshino doesn't give you love,
but you still work hard.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.790
It's just so admirable!

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.170
I'll lick you in Hoshino's place!

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.420
What's wrong?

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.130
It's nothing, but...

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:21.220
Morris and Jimmy, could you lick him, too?

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.310
You're suddenly calling us
by our TAC names?

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:24.600
Ah! I'm exposed.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.060
Exposed?

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:29.190
We've been together
ever since we came to this island,

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:32.940
so I thought maybe,
since we've gotten a little closer,

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:37.570
it would be okay to be less formal
and use your casual names...

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.700
Please, refrain from using my TAC name.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.740
I believe work and private lives
should be separate.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.200
Y-Yeah, you're right...

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.120
Please call me Lilikos.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.200
Huh?

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.420
R-Really?! I can go straight to
using your nickname?!

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.250
So can I be informal
with you, too, Hitomi?!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.090
Uh, yeah.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:59.010
Okay, okay,
since I enjoy intimacy at work,

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:00.640
please, call me by my TAC name,

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.720
Hisone!

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.760
There's no difference from before...

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:08.310
It's quite calm down there, isn't it?

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:11.850
Temperature and pressure are dropping,
and thunderclouds are forming.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.270
Everything is on schedule.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:17.650
Like the yellowtail migration preceding
the winter thunder, as said in Hokuriku.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:21.860
Hopefully, the girls will become enriched,
as the yellowtail do in winter.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:26.700
That all depends on what
Senior Master Sergeant Hoshino will do.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.330
Right, Vice-Minister Iiboshi?

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.000
I don't like seafood.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.670
Well then, what is your favorite food?

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.920
-What's with the easygoing question?
-Right now, it's kiwi.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:43.010
Looks like it's going to rain.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:45.550
Aside from that,
what exactly is this place?

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:49.100
For a deserted island,
someone built a pretty fancy torii gate.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.560
What do you think, Nao?

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:52.600
Hisone!

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.020
Please take a look at this.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:57.900
A miniature shrine?

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:01.030
And there is a picture drawn
on that wall over there.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:03.780
Is that... Masotan?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:10.370
I thought this island was chosen
for training because it was deserted,

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.920
but perhaps there is a different reason.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.210
-There you are.
-What's wrong, Hitomi?

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:22.300
Hitomi? Oh, that's me.

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:25.680
Oh! We have a problem!

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:34.600
She finally finished the raft!

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.650
But trying to get past those waves
is madness...

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.190
Hoshino! Let's stop for today!

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.490
Please come back to shore!

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:51.830
She truly intends to leave Ken behind.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:57.460
Hoshino!

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:06.140
Hoshino, let's stop, okay?

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:08.390
Leave me alone!

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:11.890
Hoshino...

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:31.490
I guess it won't lit...

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:35.120
We might not be able
to sleep here tonight.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.460
I wonder if Hoshino is okay.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.040
You know...

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.300
about Hoshino,

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:46.050
I think she's doing something awful.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.970
Poor Ken.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:50.300
Hitomi...

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.180
And yet, somehow,

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:58.560
I feel bad for Hoshino, too.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.110
I'm going to check on her.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:05.070
Please wait a moment, Hitomi.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:07.570
There is a torrential downpour outside.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:11.280
You'll be entirely soaked
before you know it and catch a cold.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:12.330
Therefore...

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:14.450
Ba-bam!

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:16.790
Oh, I get it!

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:18.500
Good thinking, Lilikos!

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.340
Even if we're soaked,
we'll be fine wearing the suit!

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:29.090
I've never felt so cold!

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:31.970
Thermal conductivity
and osmotic pressure is alarming.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.520
Did you see something on the water?

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.400
You don't think that Hoshino...

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.560
was washed away?!

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:42.940
Nao!

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.070
Nao!

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.990
-Hisone!
-Please, let me go!

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:51.070
I just misplaced Nao for a moment!

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.120
It's too dangerous!

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:56.250
She's just going back, where she belongs!

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.210
Please, Hitomi!

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.170
Let me go to her!

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:03.920
Nao...

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:05.460
Nao!

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.880
Nao!!

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.510
This isn't the time to be crying.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.180
We still haven't found Hoshino.

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:19.520
O-Oh, yeah!

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.400
To be worthy,
rescuing survivors comes first!

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:27.650
What's that sound?

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.910
This is... an afterburner?

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:33.280
Which means...

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:40.920
Ken?

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:55.300
<i>I've always admired them.</i>

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.430
GRADUATION CEREMONY

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:04.100
Wait for me, F-2!

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.700
<i>I want to prove to everyone</i>
<i>that I will be an F-2 pilot.</i>

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.080
<i>That is the...</i>

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.370
<i>reason I am here.</i>

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:46.940
An OTF?

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.070
<i>Become one with him.</i>

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:51.360
<i>Fly with him.</i>

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.110
<i>That alone is...</i>

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.240
<i>the reason why, I was born.</i>

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.830
You both saw it too?!

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:05.830
Yes!

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:09.130
There was a cute girl

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:13.550
dressed in old aviation gear
and riding an OTF.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:16.760
-I can't believe we had the same dream!
-I find it a little creepy.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.640
Hmm? Hoshino!

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:22.140
It's best not to strain yourself.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.640
But the color of your face
looks much better.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.940
Did you guys save me?

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:30.020
Nope.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:32.860
It wasn't us.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.410
Yesterday, in the pouring rain,

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:46.370
you had been pinned
beneath a pile of wood.

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.920
You couldn't move a muscle.

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.550
But Ken found you,

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:56.220
and urgently alerted us
about your whereabouts.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.640
Ken is such a good boy.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:04.480
I felt the roar of the afterburner
reverberate like a punch in the stomach.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:05.520
That's right.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.640
Who is Ken?

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:08.730
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:10.310
We're talking about F-2.

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:12.070
He is the manliest of the men.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:15.990
Don't call him some random name!
You sound like fools!

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:19.660
I didn't join the Air Self-Defense Force
just to babysit an OTF.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:20.660
Um, Hoshino--

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.990
You're satisfied as Dragon Pilots
so you wouldn't understand,

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.540
what it means, as a woman,
to dream of being a fighter pilot.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.750
The smallest mistakes aren't forgiven.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.550
Complain just a bit, and behind your back
they'll say women really are limited.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.470
Even so, the reason I could get this far

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:39.640
is because I was determined
to become an F-2 pilot.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:40.890
And yet...

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.100
Why?!

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:47.980
I've tried so hard, so why him?!

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:49.650
I...

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:51.150
wanted to fly...

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.860
a real F-2!

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.040
Ken!

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:11.710
-It's hot!
-What?

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.090
No way. Why?

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:16.130
The heat hasn't been released at all.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:17.970
It's the afterburner.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.840
To tell us about Hoshino,

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.510
he fired it up on the surface.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:27.890
What can we do?
He might die if this keeps up.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.640
Hurry and take him into the ocean!

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.150
Y-Yeah! Ken, change into
Hotel mode quickly!

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:36.650
He won't move, at all!

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:39.280
Hoshino, please say something to Ken!

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:43.660
Ken will only listen
to what you have to say!

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.160
He...

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.290
doesn't listen to what I say.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:51.420
That's not true!

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.290
-Ken is--
-During the joint training,

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:57.210
he... disregarded my orders,

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.760
and embarrassed me.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.760
That's it!

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:03.390
Hisone?

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:04.930
What's with the innocent voice?

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:08.520
So that's why he forces himself
to stay as a fighter jet.

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:09.640
Huh?

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.600
W-What are you talking about?

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:16.190
It's Ken's answer to Hoshino's wish
to become the first penguin.

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:20.150
That's the reason he's been like that.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:22.110
I see!

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.410
It seems there's some truth to that.

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:29.410
But even on this deserted island,
he maintains his constricted Foxtrot mode.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.330
If OTF do not release their heat,
they cannot live.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:34.710
That's why Ken...

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:39.960
secretly swam in the ocean
when no one was watching.

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:43.220
How did you know that?

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:46.300
When I licked Ken, he was salty.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:48.180
It was seawater!

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:51.930
You went that far, Ken?

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:53.690
Hoshino!

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:55.440
Even during the training,

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:59.610
Ken probably overheated
from working too hard!

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:01.860
No matter what happens to Ken,

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:04.110
he just wants to be
what you want, Hoshino!

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.530
That's all it is!

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:08.530
Please persuade him, Hoshino!

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:10.040
-Ken is--
-Shut up!

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:13.290
Don't make me say it over and over.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.040
Do not call him Ken!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.340
You're still saying that?

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:39.980
Hoshino!

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:42.190
Oh no! You'll get burned!

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:43.780
You fool.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.530
You are not a plane.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:48.700
You're a dragon.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:53.040
You don't need to look like this for me.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.580
You don't need to strain yourself anymore.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:00.210
It's okay to show your true self.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.000
So...

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:04.340
don't die,

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:05.300
Norma!

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:40.290
<i>It's warm in here...</i>

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:46.470
<i>even though it was</i>
<i>burning on the outside.</i>

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:55.060
<i>The first time Norma</i>
<i>swallowed me and we flew,</i>

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:56.520
<i>I was bewildered.</i>

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:58.520
<i>But...</i>

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.320
<i>my heart was dancing.</i>

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:05.320
<i>It was beating out of my chest,</i>

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.030
<i>enough to make me forget</i>
<i>my fixation on becoming a pilot.</i>

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:10.820
<i>It was just delightful.</i>

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:14.030
<i>That's right.</i>

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.410
<i>You aren't an F-2.</i>

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.000
<i>I knew that from the start.</i>

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.170
<i>Will you still...</i>

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.300
<i>fly for me?</i>

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:32.300
<i>Thank you... Norma.</i>

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.830
What's gotten into you?

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.750
They seem happy.

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:08.760
Masotan, do you want to fly too?

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.510
Magnificent!

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:17.640
El Hoshino has flipped on
the last switch for us after all.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:20.520
By realizing their love toward the OTF,

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.520
the White Lovers have become as one.

00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:25.060
This is good indeed.

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:28.530
It seems the Vice-Minister has gotten
the bounce in his step back.

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:32.320
This has also produced another outcome.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:42.000
It's beautiful, isn't it, Norma?

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.830
<i>Um, Hoshino.</i>

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:49.500
<i>Is it possible that Norma is</i>
<i>Ken's real name?</i>

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:50.920
<i>Why did you choose that name?</i>

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.300
-<i>Because it's an F-2.</i>
<i>-</i>Huh?

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:56.720
F-2, eff-two, <i>futsu.</i>

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:59.680
<i>Futsu</i> means "normal" in English.
Hence the name Norma.

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:04.690
<i>That wordplay is way too cool</i>
<i>to be a dad joke.</i>

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:07.440
<i>Norma is such a lovely name.</i>

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:09.650
<i>It fits perfectly.</i>

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:15.160
<i>So does that mean that in your heart,</i>
<i>you called it Norma instead of F-2?</i>

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:18.780
<i>Let's go, Norma!</i>

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:21.500
<i>Ah! She's flying away!</i>

00:21:30.630 --> 00:21:32.210
They're back.

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.340
Thank goodness.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:53.860
With this, we can now set our sights
on the incoming government,

00:21:54.150 --> 00:21:57.490
and take our first step into training.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:03.620
From now on, I would like your cooperation
in reporting any information.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:04.540
Huh?

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:07.170
We have not tried to conceal
anything from you, sir.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:08.790
No.

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:11.960
You concealed a very important
piece of information...

00:22:15.090 --> 00:22:17.180
the presence of the Joa lady.

00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:31.310
Seeing their smug little faces
pisses me off...

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:34.530
Hey! Give me back my head!

00:22:34.610 --> 00:22:35.900
Nao!

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:38.910
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:10.500
<i>Love.</i>

00:24:11.710 --> 00:24:13.040
<i>Love.</i>

00:24:14.330 --> 00:24:15.170
<i>Love.</i>

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:20.300
<i>It's delicious!</i>
